This is the equivalent of night vision goggles when there is no light.

1378
01:20:39,304 --> 01:20:41,345
The other thing that life has to deal with down there is the pressure.

1379
01:20:41,765 --> 01:20:44,607
The extreme pressure does have an effect on biology.

1380
01:20:45,047 --> 01:20:47,208
One thing is that it'll compress any air pockets.

1381
01:20:47,408 --> 01:20:52,511
So like swim bladders that fish use to regulate their buoyancy would get compressed significantly,

1382
01:20:53,171 --> 01:20:57,433
which is why a lot of deep sea fish don't have air pockets in their body.

1383
01:20:57,814 --> 01:21:00,915
They don't have a swim bladder, which is not, you know, there are other fish who have lost

1384
01:21:00,944 --> 01:21:06,107
swim bladders, but that is a inconvenience down that deep because air pressure is not

1385
01:21:06,207 --> 01:21:07,607
the same anymore.

1386
01:21:08,028 --> 01:21:11,009
You also have issues with biomolecules.

1387
01:21:11,409 --> 01:21:17,452
Biomolecules in the body can get deformed under such extreme pressures and stop functioning

1388
01:21:17,472 --> 01:21:17,892
correctly.

1389
01:21:18,312 --> 01:21:25,115
So a lot of deep sea fish have special chemicals or molecules that they produce in their body

1390
01:21:25,384 --> 01:21:27,565
that help fight these pressure conditions.

1391
01:21:28,145 --> 01:21:33,888
One of the common ones is often abbreviated as TMAO, which is the thing that makes fish

